  "body_html": "<h1>Derived Game</h1>\n<p>Let $S(f)$ and $T(f)$ be the optimal strategy sets of the zero-sum game\n$(S,T,f)$. The derived game of $f$ along another payoff function $g$ is the\nzero-sum game\n$$\n  (S(f),T(f),g).\n$$\nIt measures the first-order change of the value of $f$ in the direction $g$.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 3.4, after Prop. 3.4.2] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. The game (S(f), T(f), g) is called the derived game of f along g.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
